## History:
##		- 20260318 JC: Created.
##		- 20260326 JC: Only `mount /boot/efi`, not `mount -a`.
##		- 20260327 JC: Fixed a logic error that was preventing proper mounting.
##		- 20260813 JC: Rewritten as a standalone systemd-invoked executable.
##			- Was sourced into the shared '/etc/rc.local' shell via '/etc/rc.localx9.d/020-insure-efi-mount'.
##			  That wrapper is retired (kept under 'legacy/' in the repo); this now runs from
##			  'tkz-insure-efi-mount.service', which also removes the need for the old 'sleep 5' since
##			  systemd orders it properly instead of guessing.
##			- No longer calls 'sudo' while already root (which was opening a PAM session per command);
##			  instead it re-executes via sudo only when actually invoked by a non-root user.
##			- Mountpoint is now an argument rather than hardcoded, and the mount unit name is derived
##			  from it with 'systemd-escape', so this works for any mountpoint.
##			- Prefers 'systemctl start <unit>.mount' over bare 'mount', and reports when the mount unit
##			  is masked - which is the actual root cause of needing this script at boot.
##			- Added '--check' (probe, no changes), '--dry-run' and '--wait'; real exit codes throughout.
##			- Replaced the repeated flag-recomputation blocks with single-purpose state predicates.
##•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••
